  "content": "{section: Intro}\n[G] [Am7] [C/B] [C] [C] [C/B] [G] [C] [C] [C/B] [G] [D]\n\n{section: Verso 1}\n[G] [Am7] [C/B] [C] [C/B] [G] [C] [C/B] [G] [D]\nDown, fall by the wayside no getting out\n[G] [Am7] [C/B] [C] [C/B] [G] [C] [C/B] [G] [D]\nDown, cry me a river dried up and dammed\n[C]The names can be changed but the [D]place is still the same\n[Em]I am loaded, [Bm]told that all's for naught, [C]holds me [Am7]down\n\n{section: Solo}\n[G] [Am7] [C/B] [C] [C/B] [G] [C] [C/B] [D] (x2)\n\n{section: Verso 2}\n[G] [Am7] [C/B] [C] [C/B] [G] [C] [C/B] [G] [D]\nRise, life is in motion I'm stuck in line\n[G] [Am7] [C/B] [C] [C/B] [G] [C] [C/B] [G] [D]\nRise, you can't be neutral on a moving train\n[C]One day the symptoms fade think I'll throw these [D]pills away\n[Em]And if hope could [Bm]grow from dirt like [C]me, it can be [A]done [G]\n\n{section: Ponte}\n[Em]Won't let the light escape from [A]me [C]\n[Em]Won't let the darkness swallow [A]me [C]\n\n{section: Outro}\n[G] [Am7] [C/B] [C] [C/B] [G] [C] [C/B] [D] (x7)\n[G] [D] [G] [D] (x4)"
